2 CONT
2 CONT http://drouillard.us/drouillard_frontiersmens_line
2 CONT
2 CONT http://yelnam.tripod.com/Drouillard.html
2 CONT
2 CONT Their son, Simon dit Argentcourt Drouillard was born on Nov 10th 1669 and baptized  at St. Pierre Church, in Marennes, France on November 11, 1668. His Godparents were Simon Chaudart and Marie Dumas.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1684
2 CONT
2 CONT Simon dit Argentcourt Drouillard came to New France (1.) as a soldier with Lestringant de Saint-Martin (2.) and was in the campaign against the Iroquois below Montreal. Simons is listed as a soldier in the Marines, a ship's carpen
2 CONC ter, and a day laborer.
2 CONT ----
2 CONT http://ihavegreatgenes.blogspot.com/2014/03/simon-drouillard-dit-argentcourt.html
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT Many sources on the Internet list Simon as having been buried on Oct 21, 1733. The source for this seems to be the Dennison genealogy, but there is no record of his death or burial in the records of Ste. Anne. The sources on the I
2 CONC nternet go on to say that Simon was killed by an Iroquois ambush 3 miles from Detroit. I have found no published source for this.
2 CONT === GEDCOM Source ===
