1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Marie Lasnon was a Fille du Roi. Between 1663 and 1673, some 768 Filles du Roi or "King's Daughters" emigrated to New France under the sponsorship of the French government as part of the overall strategy of strengt
2 CONC hening the colony until it could stand on its own without economic and military dependence on France. It is recorded that Marie, married Pierre Feret, Nov. 24, 1667.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://drouillard.us/history_of_the_drouillards
2 CONT
2 CONT Between 1634 and 1662; 262 young ladies braved the elements to begin an uncertain future in the backwoods of Canada.
2 CONT
