1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://drouillard.us/our_family
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes 	
2 CONT
2 CONT     In 1733, the family was living at Soulanges. Between 1741-1744 they were at St. Joseph-de-la-Riviere-des-Prairies. In 1746 they were back at Lachine. Jean Baptiste moved his family to Detroit 26 Jul 1749 where he had received 
2 CONC a land grant of three arpents on the south shore of the river.
2 CONT
2 CONT     We know that Jean Baptiste died sometime between March 1754 and the middle of 1755, so there has been speculation that he was part of Beaujeu's force that fought at Fort Duquesne in 1755. [SK]
2 CONT
2 CONT Children 	
2 CONT >	1. Jean Baptiste Amable Drouillard, b. 09 Nov 1731, d. 02 Jan 1788, River Raisin, Monroe, Michigan 
2 CONT
2 CONT >	2. Simon Amable Drouillard, b. 03 Mar 1734, d. 25 Jul 1805
2 CONT >	3. Marie Elisabeth Drouillard, b. About 1735, d. 03 Jun 1783
2 CONT
2 CONT >	4. Francois Drouillard, b. 11 Apr 1741, d. 23 Sep 1812
2 CONT
2 CONT >	5. Joseph Drouillard, b. 1740-42, Des Cedres  , d. 25 Jan 1783
2 CONT
2 CONT  	6. Antoine Drouillard, b. 22 Feb 1743, d. 10 Sep 1767
2 CONT
2 CONT >	7. Marie Catherine Drouillard, b. 16 Sep 1744, bur. May 1771, Assumption, South Coast of Detroit Find all individuals with events at this location
2 CONT
2 CONT >	8. Pierre Drouillard, b. 11 Oct 1746, d. 14 Apr 1803
2 CONT
2 CONT  	9. Marie Francoise Drouillard, b. 02 May 1750, bur. 30 May 1750, Ste. Anne of Detroit 
2 CONT
2 CONT  	10. Pierre Drouillard, b. 23 Apr 1751, bur. 26 Apr 1751, Ste. Anne of Detroit 
2 CONT
2 CONT  	11. Antoine Drouillard, b. 10 Mar 1753, d. 09 Aug 1764
2 CONT --------------------
