1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''https://www.familysearch.org/en/tree/person/about/LRGY-K7Q
2 CONT Brief Life History of Marie Madeleine'''
2 CONT
2 CONT When Marie Madeleine Cadoret was born on 2 November 1725, in Saint-Pierre-de-L'Île-d'Orléans, L'Île-d'Orléans, Quebec, Canada, her father, Pierre Cadoret, was 28 and her mother, Charlotte Maranda, was 28. 
2 CONT
2 CONT She married Louis Corbet on 2 February 1751, in Notre-Dame de Québec, Quebec City, Quebec, Canada. They were the parents of at least 3 sons. 
2 CONT Jean Baptiste Corbet 1751–
2 CONT Pierre Henri Corbet 1754–
2 CONT Paul-Hippolyte Corbeil 1756–1828
2 CONT
2 CONT After Louis's death in 1756, she married Jean-Joseph Pothier on 26 October 1760, in Pointe-du-Lac, Francheville, Quebec, Canada. They were the parents of at least 2 sons and 3 daughters. 
2 CONT Marie Josephe Pothier 1761–
2 CONT Marie Charlotte Poitier 1762–1851
2 CONT Claire Pothier 1764–1777
2 CONT Joseph Etienne Pothier 1766–
2 CONT Joseph Pothier 1769–1820
2 CONT
2 CONT She died on 18 December 1788, in Canada East, British North America, at the age of 63, and was buried in Saint-Paul, Joliette, Quebec, Canada.
