1 NOTE {geni:about_me} André Rapin dit Skaianis
2 CONT Adopted child of Andre Rapin and Clemence Jarry.
2 CONT
2 CONT Detroit River Region métis Families Compiled by Diane Wolford Sheppard states:
2 CONT Anne Gourdon, widow of Pierre Lelat, married André Rapin dit Skianis, a panis who had been adopted by André Rapin and Clémence Jarry, 18 April 1706.
2 CONT Their son, André Rapin dit Skianis, married Marie Anne Domitille Parent in August 1744 at Michilimackinac.
2 CONT Their son, André Rapin dit Skianis, married Madeleine Casse dite Saint-Aubin 2 February 1778 in Ste. Anne du Détroit.
2 CONT --
2 CONT Who and What Were the Panis Indians Buried from Ste. Anne de Detroit? Suzanne Boivin Sommerville states:
2 CONT Panis (or pany, which provides a clue to pronunciation) and panisse (feminine form) are French language versions of the name of the Pawnee Indians (from what is now Nebraska, on the Missouri River) who were taken as slaves by othe
2 CONC r Indians.
2 CONT https://www.familysearch.org/tree/person/details/LC1T-RZ9
2 CONT ----
