1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://www.gphistorical.org/pdf-files/historicaldocs/provencaladopts.pdf
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.gphistorical.org/proweir.html
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT LifeSketch:	Last names in CAPS are linked with family on Find a Grave
2 CONT
2 CONT Peter Provonsal
2 CONT BIRTH	1795
2 CONT DEATH	1869 (aged 73–74)
2 CONT BURIAL	
2 CONT Mount Elliott Cemetery
2 CONT Detroit, Wayne County, Michigan, USA 
2 CONT PLOT	Section A Lot 180
2 CONT MEMORIAL ID	65588190 · View Source
2 CONT
2 CONT PROVONSAL (PROVENCAL), PETER (PIERRE)
2 CONT b. 1795 d. 1869.
2 CONT Bur. Sec. A, Lot 180.
2 CONT
2 CONT Left the mercantile business in 1819 because of failing health, and bought land in Grosse Pointe so he could farm in the country. He built a French farmhouse at the foot of what is presently Provencal Road in Grosse Pointe Shores.
2 CONC  At the age of 36, he married 18-year-old Euphemia St. Aubin. Having no children of their own, they eventually founded a school in their home for children orphaned by the cholera epidemics of the 1830s and 1840s. A confessional bo
2 CONC x and an altar were built in their parlor, which served as a church for a while. After 14 years of marriage, they had a daughter, Catherine, who eventually married Judge James Weir. About 1900, the old farmhouse was moved to Kerch
2 CONC eval Avenue near Lakeview, and is known today as the Weir house. Provencal Road in Grosse Pointe is named in honor of Pierre and his wife, Euphemia.
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: Mt Elliott Cemetery, A History, Est. 1841 p 74
