1 OCCU Ancêtre en Nouvelle France - il est confirmé le 1662-05-01, Québec
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Born on January 24,1638 in St. Georges d'Oleron, Saintes, Saintonge, France.(See Note 1) Immigration year to Canada is unknown. (See Note 2) Married Barbe Hallay or Hale on November 4, 1670 in Notre Dame-de-Quebec,
2 CONC  Quebec, Canada. Had four children IGNACE PHILIPPE born in 1671; Marie Anne, 1674-XXXX (See Note 3); Charles, 1678-1740; and Jean, 1682-1749. Died after November 19, 1715 Quebec, Canada (See Note 4).
2 CONT
2 CONT Source:
2 CONT
2 CONT Beth W. Davies 
2 CONT
2 CONT American Fork, Utah 
2 CONT
2 CONT June 2008
2 CONT
2 CONT Research Notes:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1..Since the Family History Library in Salt Lake City, Utah parish records for St. Georges d'Oleron do not begin until 1651, Jean's birth date was taken from the PRDH database. A database called Fichier Origine,www.fichierorigine.
2 CONC com, which is attempting to trace the French origins of the original immigrants to Quebec, is the source of his birth date.  
2 CONT
2 CONT 2.Jean Carrier and Barbe Hale (Hallay) were the original Carrier family in Quebec.
2 CONT
2 CONT 3.Marie Anne's death record could not be found. Genealogy of Canada, www.ourorigins.org., reported her death date as June 3, 1705 in Lauzon, Levis, Quebec. However, there are for 1705 for Lauzon no parish copy of the records at th
2 CONC e Family History Library in Salt Lake City, Utah and in the Drouin collection of parish records. The PRDH database did not list a burial date for her.   
2 CONT
2 CONT 4.Jean's death record could not be located. Genealogy of Canada, www.ourorigins.org, and The Family History Library, www.familysearch.org, reported Jean's death date as April 20,1711, Lauzon, Levis,Quebec, Canada whereas Fichier O
2 CONC rigine, www.fichierorigine.com, reported his death as after November 19, 1715. Jean Baptiste Carrier, grandson of Jean, was born on April 20, 1711.Since his and his grandson's first name were Jean, Genealogy of Canada could have m
2 CONC ade a transcription error. Also, an unidentified source has Jean entering into a contract (terms undisclosed) with his sons Charles and Jean on November 19,1715. This could be the reason Fichier Origine reported Jean Carrier's's d
2 CONC eath date as after November 19, 1715.
