1 NOTE {geni:about_me} BARBE HALAY was born about 1645 in St. Julien de Coudray, Orleans, Chartres, France. She died in Jun 1696 in Lauzon, Levis, P. Q.. She was buried on 18 Jun 1696 in St. Joseph de La Pointe de Levis, P. Q.. She was a
2 CONC lso known as Hallay , Halay & Halle. Parents: JEAN-BAPTISTE SR. HALAY and MATHURINE VALLET.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was married to JEAN CARRIER on 4 Nov 1670 in Notre Dame de Quebec, Quebec City, P. Q.. Children were: IGNACE-PHILIPPE CARRIER, Marie-Anne CARRIER, Sr. Charles (1) CARRIER , Jean CARRIER, Louise #1 CARRIER, Louise # 2 CARRIER.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Born  circa 1646 in St. Julien, Coudray, Chartres, France. Immigrated to Canada in 1659 (See Note 1) Married Jean Carrier (Carie) on November 4, 1670 in Notre Dame-de-Quebec, Quebec, Canada. (See Note 2) Had four children IGNACE P
2 CONC HILIPPE born in 1671; Marie Anne, 1674-XXXX (See Note 4); Charles, 1678-1740; and Jean 1682-1749. Died in Lauzon , Levis, Quebec, Canada on June 16,1696.
2 CONT
2 CONT Source:
2 CONT
2 CONT Beth W. Davies
2 CONT
2 CONT American Fork, Utah
2 CONT
2 CONT June 2008 
2 CONT
2 CONT Research Notes:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.At the end of the summer of 1658, Barbe's father Jean Baptiste returned to France and in 1659 returned to Canada with Barbe, her mother Mathurine Valet, and her two sisters Marie and Elisabeth. Marie was their oldest child and a
2 CONC t age 18 made her Confirmation in August of 1659. This suggests that Barbe's parents were married in France before 1641. ( Nos Ancetres, "Jean Baptiste Halle", by Gerard Lebel, Chapter 9, Page 88, Sante Anne de Beaupre 1993.) 
2 CONT
2 CONT 2.Ten years prior to her marriage to Jean Carrier, Barbe Hale, age 15, was possessed by the devil. She was placed under the guardianship of Mother Catherine de Saint-Augustin. (See Note 3) After several attempts at exorcism, the e
2 CONC vil angel was finally driven out. (The Genealogist, "The Demonic Possession of Barbe Hallay", by Henri Carrier, Volume 12, Number 2, Issue No.28, Spring 1986.)    
2 CONT
2 CONT 3.Catherine de Saint-Augustin , 1632-1668, was beatified on Easter Sunday, April 23, 1989, by Pope Paul II.
2 CONT
2 CONT 4.Marie's death record could not be found. Genealogy of Canada, www.ourorigins.org., reported her death date as June 3, 1705 in Lauzon, Levis, Quebec. However, there are for 1705 for Lauzon no parish copy of the records at the Fam
2 CONC ily History Library in Salt Lake City, Utah and in the Drouin collection of parish records.  The PRDH database did not list a burial date for her.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT aussi connue sous le nom de Barbe Palloy, Barbe Halé 6, Barbe Halay 5, Barbe Hallé 4, Barbe Hallay 2, 3 et Étiennette-Barbe Halay 1.
2 CONT
2 CONT Elle est la fille de Mathurine Valet 5, 7 et Jean-Baptiste Halay 7, 8.
2 CONT
2 CONT Elle est baptisée en 1645 en France 14, 15, 16, 17. Barbe Palloy étudie entre au pensonnariat de l'Hôtel-Dieu de Québec en 1661 6. Barbe Palloy est servante de Jean Maheu en 1666 à Québec, Capitale-Nationale, Québec, Canada 1. Bar
2 CONC be Palloy, Jacques Jore, Louis Maheut, Jean-Paul Maheu, Jean Maheu et Marguerite Corriveau résident à Québec en 1666 1. Jean Carrier et Barbe Palloy signent un contrat de mariage le 27 juillet 1670 par devant Sieur Pierre Duquet d
2 CONC e la Chenaye n présence de Louis Gezeron dit Brulot, André Albert dit Laroche, Sieur Guillaume Albert de Lafontaine et Sieur François Bissot de la Rivière 4. Elle épouse Jean Carrier fils de Jeanne Dodier et Jean Carrier le 4 nove
2 CONC mbre 1670 à Québec 2, 18, 19. Marie-Anne Carriere, Charles Carriere, Ignace Carriere, Barbe Girard, Barbe Palloy et Jean Carrier résident à la seigneurie de Lauzon, Chaudière-Appalaches, Québec en 1681 2, 20. Elle décède le 18 jui
2 CONC n 1696 à Lévis, Chaudière-Appalaches 4. Elle est inhumée le 18 juin 1696 à Saint-Joseph, Lévis 8, 21.
2 CONT
2 CONT Elle est présente lors de la signature du contrat de mariage de Marie-Marguerite Maranda et Jean Halay le 24 juin 1682 à Lauzon, Chaudière-Appalaches 17.
2 CONT
2 CONT Liste de ses enfants connus:
2 CONT
2 CONT + 1. Ignace Carriere (1671 - 1765) 2, 9, 10 (de Jean Carrier) + 2. Charles Carriere (1678 - 1740) 2, 4, 10 (de Jean Carrier) + 3. Marie-Anne Carriere (1674 - 1705) 2, 3, 11 (de Jean Carrier)
2 CONT    4. Louise Carrier 10, 12 (de Jean Carrier) + 5. Jean Carrier (1682 - 1749) 10, 13 (de Jean Carrier) 1. Internet - Recensement de 1666 en Nouvelle-France, référant au tome IV, chapitre IV du livre Histoire des Canadiens-Français
2 CONC  de Benjamin Sulte, compilé par Jean-Guy Sénécal (senecal@fmed.ulaval.ca) le 17 mars 1998.
2 CONT
