1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Born on August 14, 1738 in Lauzon , Levis, Quebec, Canada. Married Catherine Begin on January 10 ,1764 in Lauzon. (See Note 1) Had eight children all of whom were born in Lauzon Jean Baptiste born in 1765-1830 ; IG
2 CONC NACE, 1766;  Catherine, 1769-1845; Marie Louise, 1771-1811; Genevieve, 1773-1776; Agathe Angelique, 1775-1831 (See Note 2) Joseph,  1778-1787; and Charles, 1780-1810. Died in Lauzon on December 9, 1829.
2 CONT
2 CONT Source:
2 CONT
2 CONT Beth W. Davies
2 CONT
2 CONT American Fork, Utah
2 CONT
2 CONT March 2008
2 CONT
2 CONT Research Notes:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.They were married by Father Charles d'Youville Dufrost. He was the son of Saint Margurite d'Youville, 1701-1771. She was the founder of the Sisters of Charity, the "Grey Nuns of Canada". Canonized by John Paul 11 in 1990. She wa
2 CONC s the first native Canadian to be elevated to sainthood. 
