1 NOTE {geni:about_me} The NORMAND and GASPARD families of Avoyelles share the same family roots. Both surnames revolve around one Jean Gaspard Normand . Jean Gaspard Normand's parents were both natives of Quebec. His paternal grandfathe
2 CONC r, Jean le Normand , was born in 1638 at Dige, Normandy. He was  the first of that family in Canada. He was the son of Gervais leNormand and Leonore Janet. Jean's paternal grandmother was Anne leLaboureur, daughter of Thomas le La
2 CONC boureur and Margueri te Bardin.They were from Caen, Normandy. Jean le Normand and Anne were married at Quebec on July 18, 1656.
2 CONT
2 CONT Jean Gaspard Normand's mother, Francoise Jean, was born at Quebec,daughter of Denis Jean and Marie Peltier. Denis Jean was the son of Elie Jean and Elizabeth Lambade (Lambert) of Saint onge. Marie'sparents were Nicolas Peltier and
2 CONC  Jeanne Voisy of St. Pierre deGallardon Parish , Beauce in Orleanais.
2 CONT
2 CONT Jean Gaspard Normand was born in 1712. He married on February 14,1734, Marie-Josephe Chenier at Bout-de-l'Isle, Montreal.Marie-Josephe was the daughter of Joseph Chenier and Magdelein eDuboc. Jean Gaspard Normand, his wife, and fo
2 CONC ur sons ( Jean Pierre,Daniel, Joseph, and Laurent ) moved from Canada to St. CharlesParish, Louisiana, in about 1765.
2 CONT
2 CONT Daniel "Gaspard" Normand , born around 1750, married at St. Charles sometime between 1770-1773 Francoise Materne called Jean des Jean. She was born at Natchitoches Post on June 29, 1755 , the daughter of Jean Mader called Jean des
2 CONC  Jean and his wife, Marie Thiley. Jean Mader died at Natchitoches on April 21, 1758. His wife died there on March 20, 1761. It is apparent that after Marie Thiley's death, her minor children (including Francoise) moved to St. Char
2 CONC les Parish to live with relatives. This is how Francoise came to meet and marry Daniel.There were seven children born to this couple. Daniel and family, along with his brother Jean Pierre , came to Avoyelles from the GermanCoast i
2 CONC n about 1790. After the move, Daniel called himself "Gaspard" and Jean Pierre retained the surname "Normand". The children and grandchildren of Daniel used the "Gaspard" name exclusively.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://louisianalineage.com/b197.htm
