1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Jeanne Merrin livedin Canada, Nouvelle-France.The Jarry family were one of the early settlers of Montreal. The Grande Recrue, Jeanne Mance, took money that was intended for the local hospital and used it to recruit
2 CONC  a hundred people, of which, they were a part. The contingent arrived at Ville-Marie (Montreal) on November 16, 1653. Of the 95 who embarked from Saint-Nazaire, France, 24 are killed by Iroquois, 4 drown, and one burnt when his ho
2 CONC use catches fire. In 1689, the English–allied Iroquois attacked the Island of Montreal, killing many.
2 CONT * Reference: [https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Merrin-8 WikiTree Genealogy] - [http://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Sep 29 2020, 16:24:18 UTC''
2 CONT https://www.familysearch.org/tree/person/details/9VCL-NCV
