1 NOTE {geni:about_me} On 10-15-1788, Louis Mommini and his father (Louis) sold Fr. Frechette, pastor of St. Anne, Detroit, land 1 arpent and 2 perches wide along the St-Antoine, Riviere aux Raisins (Monroe, MI) and 40 arpents deep, for 
2 CONC 400 pounds. This was the site of the original St-Antoine, Riviere aux Raisins (Monroe, MI) Church. Payments were made in farm products. It was paid in full on 5-25-1790. This property was referred to as Claim # 648.
2 CONT
2 CONT ------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT According to Talcott E. Wing's book " The History of Monroe County Michigan", "The first white settlers in the township (Erie) were Hycinthe Bernard and Louis Momenee, about 1800."
2 CONT
2 CONT -----------------------------------
