2 CONT Louis Mominee and his brother, Baptiste signed a petition to the U.S. Congress on December 27, 1816 asking for compensation for grevious loses in the Raisin River massacre. On October 18, 1819, he and his brother Peter signed anot
2 CONC her petition asking for the land they had lived on to be granted to them for losses sustained in connection with the War of 1812. Louis was a private in Captain Anderson's Company of the 2nd Regiment of Michigan Militia. In 1827, 
