1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.familysearch.org/en/tree/person/about/LTC5-FPN
2 CONT Brief Life History of Pierre
2 CONT
2 CONT Born January 4, 1668  in Quebec, Canada to parents Jacques Enaud/Henault (1636-1690) and Marie Leroux (1645-1717).
2 CONT
2 CONT Married Marie Anne Ratelle (1670–1711) on 3 février 1688
2 CONT in Saint-Pierre-de-Sorel, Pierre-De Saurel, Québec, Canada
2 CONT They had at least 2 sons and 5 daughters
2 CONT Pierre Henault dit Delorme 1691–1756
2 CONT Pierre Hénault dit Fresnier/Freniere 1694–1756
2 CONT Marie Marguerite Henault 1696–1741
2 CONT Marie Jeanne Hénault 1698–1770
2 CONT Marie Thérèse Hénault 1700–1782
2 CONT Marie Louise Hénault 1705–1731
2 CONT Marie Geneviève Henault Canada 1709–1740
2 CONT
2 CONT Died on   5 May 1711 (aged 41–42)  in Quebec, Canada (Reportedly killed by the Les Renards tribe.
2 CONT --------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT On his way from Fort Pontchartrain to Michillimakinac he was killed by Indians from the tribe known as the "Foxes ("Les Renards") on June 2, 1715.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.nosorigines.qc.ca/GenealogieQuebec.aspx?pid=150961
2 CONT ----
2 CONT Pierre is the son of Jacques-Pierre Henault dit Canada. He was born about 1669, in Sorel. Pierre married Marie Ann Ratel in February 1688, in Sorel-Tracy. They are the parents of the following (verified with PRDH):
2 CONT 1) 1) Pierre (1691- ) md Marie-Marguerite Piette dit Lafreniere
2 CONT 2) Pierre (1694-1756) md Marie-Genevieve Genereaux
2 CONT 3) Marie (1696-1741) md (a) Charles Boucher and (b) Mathurin Goulet
2 CONT 4) Marie-Jeanne (1698-1770) md Pierre Emery dit Codere
2 CONT 5) Marie-Therese (1700-1782) md Jean-Baptiste Martin dit St-Jean
2 CONT 6) Marie-Anne (abt 1702-1782) md Jean-Baptiste Savignac
2 CONT 7) Marie-Louise (abt 1705-1731) md Jean-Baptiste Boyer dit LaFantaisie
2 CONT 8) Marie-Genevieve (1709-1740) md Francois Robidoux
2 CONT
2 CONT He was a Carignan Soldier.
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/124454677/pierre-henault
2 CONT ----
2 CONT http://geninfo.org/en/dit_canada.htm
