2 CONT Brief Life History of Elisabeth Isabelle
2 CONT
2 CONT When Elisabeth Isabelle Leroux Rousson was born in 1738, in Quebec, Canada, her father, Jean Baptiste Rousson dit Leroux, was 33 and her mother, Marie Angelique Elisabeth Libersan, was 27. 
2 CONT
2 CONT She married 1st husband Francois Amable Martin dit St-Jean (1734-1778) on 12 February 1759, in Saint-Joseph-de-Soulanges, Lower Canada, British North America. 
2 CONT They were the parents of at least 4 sons and 6 daughters. 
2 CONT Marie Isabelle Martin 1760–1760 (died in infancy)
2 CONT Marguerite Martin dite St-Jean 1761–1804
2 CONT Francois Martin Dit St.Jean 1762–1817
2 CONT Marie Joseph Martin St. Jean 1764–
2 CONT Pierre Martin dit St Jean 1766–1769 (died in infancy)
2 CONT Charles Martin dit St-Jean 1768–1840
2 CONT Amable Martin 1769–1844
2 CONT Suzanne Martin dit St-Jean 1772–1819
2 CONT Jean Baptiste Martin dit St Jean 1773–1773 (died in infancy)
2 CONT Marie Amable Martin St-Jean 1777–1860
2 CONT
2 CONT She married 2nd husband Joseph Houde/Houle (1749– )
2 CONT on 22 April 1781 in Saint-Joseph-de-Soulanges, Soulanges, Québec, Canada
2 CONT They had at least 6 sons and 4 daughters
2 CONT Charles Houle 1768–1840
2 CONT Joseph HOULE 1777–1820
2 CONT Martin Houde Houle 1782–1865
2 CONT Eustache Houle 1783–1832
2 CONT Marie Angelique Houle 1784–
2 CONT Catherine Houle 1785–1786
2 CONT Veronique Houle 1787–1788 (died in infancy)
2 CONT Marie Josephte Houle 1787–
2 CONT Louis HOULE 1793–
2 CONT Francois HOULE 1796–
2 CONT
2 CONT She died on 4 March 1829, in Saint-Polycarpe, Soulanges, Quebec, Canada, at the age of 91, and was buried in Saint-Polycarpe, Soulanges, Quebec, Canada.
2 CONT
2 CONT
