2 ADDR
1 DEAT
2 DATE ABT 15 AUG 1768
2 PLAC Detroit, Wayne, Michigan, USA
2 ADDR
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Excerpt from Tales of the Forgotten Village, by W.P. Sugars:
2 CONT
2 CONT "... In 1750, Pierre, Ambrose, Augustine, and Marguerite paddled westward [from Petite Riviere] with their families. Pierre with six children and the other two boys with four each, to Grand Marais [Great Swamp] on the shore of Lac
2 CONC  Sainte Claire. All four had been married at Baie Saint Paul, Québec, a little village resting in the shadow of a round hill that rises from the end of a narrow peninsula in the delta of the St. Lawrence [River]. Pierre Tremblay h
2 CONC ad married Madeleine Simard in March, 1733; Augustine had married Marie Judith La Forest, February 13, 1741; Ambrose had married Marguerite Simard, sister of Madeleine, January 20, 1744; and Marguerite completed the group on May 2
2 CONC 3, 1746 by marrying Guillaume La Forest, brother of Marie Judith. In 1760, parents Michel Tremblay and Genevieve Bouchard paddled from Quebec to meet them."
2 CONT
2 CONT * Marriage to William Laforest: (23 May 1746 — Age: 21) Baie St Paul , Quebec
2 CONT * Burial: (15 Aug 1768 — Age: 43) Detroit , Michiagn** Updated from [http://trees.ancestry.com/tree/31520784/person/18061454596 Ancestry Genealogy] via daughter [http://www.geni.com/profile-34669802159 Marie-Archange Laforest] by 
2 CONC [http://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Feb 8 2015, 20:03:42 UTC''
