2 CONT Details copied from the Seguin D`Amerique Website - Page entitled `Famille de Francois Seguin et de Jeanne Petit (ancetres de la plupart des Seguin d`Amerique)................Children of Joseph Seguin dit Laderoute and Francoise S
2 CONC auvage i Marie Anne Seguin dit Laderoute; b. June 21, 1724 in Champlain, Quebec, Canada; m. Antoine Gilbert Sanspeur July 13; m. Jacques Devegnais dit Tullier, son of Nicholas Devegnais dit Tullier and Dorothee Mercier on January 
2 CONC 7, 1761 in Immaculate Conception Catholic Church, Kaskaskia, Illinois Country (later Illinois); d. September 14, 1776 in Kaskaskia, Illinois Country (later Illinois) at age 52 ii Cajetan Seguin; b. January 23, 1724/25 in Detroit, 
2 CONC Michigan; m. Marie-Genevieve Tremblay, daughter of Pierre Tremblay and Marie Madeleine Simard on January 8, 1758 in Detroit, Michigan iii Alexis Seguin dit Laderoute; b. March 22, 1732/33 in Detroit, Wayne Co., Michigan; m. Marie-
2 CONC Agathe Campau, daughter of Charles Campau and Marie-Agathe Casse dit Aubin on January 30, 1757 in Detroit, Wayne Co., Michigan iv Jacques Seguin; m. Marie-Rose Thuillier, daughter of Nicholas Devegnais dit Tullier and Dorothee Mer
2 CONC cier on February 3, 1752 in Kaskaskia, Illinois Country (later Illinois); d. On 14 November 1768 the bones of Jacques Seguin were found near Kaskaskia. He was assumed killed by savages. v Pierre Seguin; m. Marie-Louise Devegnais d
2 CONC it Thuillier, daughter of Nicholas Devegnais dit Tullier and Dorothee Mercier on January 17, 1764 in Kaskaskia, Illinois Country (later Illinois) vi Jeanne Seguin....................."Joseph, baptise a Boucherville le 13 Septembre
2 CONC  1694, il epouse a Detroit, le 12 Avril 1723, Francoise Sauvage, fille de Jacques Sauvage et de Marie-Catherine Jean. Il est l`ancetre des Seguin du sud-ouest ontarien et du Michigan des Etats-Unis d`Amerique, dont certains on gar
2 CONC de le surnom de Laderoute."......................As per document attached to photos ; "Joseph Seguin dit Laderoute born 13 September 1694 Boucherville, burried 29 April 1793 in Detroit Michigan, married 12 April 1723 Frances Sauva
2 CONC ge, born 2 February 1799 Cahmplain, burried 31 July 1792 Detroit, daughter of James Sauvage and Catherine Jean dit Vien : Their children born Detroit are: (1)Mary Jane born 21 June 1724, m 29 July 1742 to Anthony Meny born 1712, b
2 CONC urried 1 February 1794 Detroit, son of Claude Meny and Mary de Niger (2)Cajetan born 23 January 1726,(3) James born 8 May 1727,(4) Mary Frances born 24 December 1728, burried 18 January 1729,(5) Joseph born 11 May 1730, burried 23
2 CONC  September 1751, (6)Charles born 54 February, burried 10 February 1732, (7)Alexis born 22 March 1733, (8)John Baptist born 13 November and burried 24 November 1735, (9)Peter born 6 January 1741 and burried 14 March 1802 (10)Mary b
2 CONC orn 30 April 1744)... - FROM: http://theseguintree.tribalpages.com
2 CONT
