1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes for Peter (Pierre) Meny:
2 CONT
2 CONT From: "ST. CLAIR COUNTY, MICHIGAN: ITS HISTORYAND ITS PEOPLE", pg. 71. "When proceedings were taken before the land board in 1808, there was little formality. Each claimant was required to file a claim stating, in general terms, i
2 CONC ts location, boundries and amount of land included. In most cases the claim was in terms of arpents of land. Thus, on July 1, 1808 Pierre (Peter) Mini (Meny) entered his claim for a tract of land on the St. Clair River as: Detroit
2 CONC , July 1,1808 to Peter Audrain, Register of the land office at Detroit. Sir: Take notice that I now enter with the Commissioners of the Land Office at Detroit my claim to a tract of land situated on the River St. Clair, containing
2 CONC  six arpents in front by forty in depth, bounded in front by said River St. Clair, in the rear by unconceeded lands, above by Francoise Chartier and below by unconceeded lands. I claim and I set up title by virtue of long possessi
2 CONC on, occupancy and improvements made by me on those from whom I derive title."
2 CONT
2 CONT Pierre Mini (his mark). Witness: Peter Audrain
2 CONT
2 CONT #202 Pierre Mini, 6 arpents by 40. Allowed on testimony that claimant had been in possession for more than 20 years. He was also on the tax role for 1802.
2 CONT
2 CONT #202 Pierre Mini, 6 arpents by 40. Allowed on testimony of Antoine Nicholas Petit as to requisite possession.
2 CONT
2 CONT From: "FIRST LAND OWNERS OF ST. CLAIR COUNTY, MICHIGAN", Hilda A. Taylor, 1978 Michigan Genealogical Council.
2 CONT
2 CONT Private Claims #202: Town 2N, Range 16E, 202.43 acres Pierre Mini.
2 CONT
2 CONT Private Claims #203: Town 1N, Range 15E, 233 acres Pierre Mini.
2 CONT
2 CONT From: "HISTORY OF ST. CLAIR COUNTY, MICHIGAN" A.T. Andeas & Co., Chicago, Illinois. Pub. 1883. Pg. 222: "Land claim 202 July 1808 Pierre Mini claimed 240 French acres south of Joseph Bassinet's tract, north of F. Chartier and fron
2 CONC ting on the river, in his possession since 1786 or, for over twenty years previous to July 1, 1808 according to Col. Cotteral. Land Claim #203 July 1808 Pierre Mini claimed 240 arpents fronting on the river, below Francoise Charti
2 CONC er's lands, proven by Antoine Petit to be in claimants possession previous to 1706."
2 CONT
2 CONT From the research of Richard G, Cottrell: Peter (Pierre) was recorded in the St. Clair County census of Sept., 1796. "In 1808, when ownership claims to the land were being re-established by the US Govt., the family land was reacqu
2 CONC ired along the channel leading into Lake St. Clair, just west of Algonac via private claims # 202 (202 acres) and 203 (233 acres). In the Cherry Beach area via claim # 204 (305) acres. He was also a Lieut. in the St. Clair Territo
2 CONC rial Milita during 1805-1806. Marie was recorded in Macomb Cty. Mich. in the 1820 census. '
2 CONT
2 CONT From: "THE CATHOLIC CHURCH IN DETROIT 1701-1888" Published 1951. "The earliest Church in St Clair County was St. Félicité built in 1826 about 2mi. below Marine City. The baptismal register, whose entries are signed by Fr. Andreas 
2 CONC Viszoczky in 1833, is preserved in the St Clair Parish records & Fr. Otto Skolla, before beginning his enteries in May 1843, inscribes a heading: Children baptized in the church of St. Félicité in St. Clair - 1845 church given new
2 CONC  name - St. Agatha." It is interesting to note that the location of the land claim by Peter Meny, noted above, is thought to be very close the land donated for the building of St. Félecité by "G. Cottrell & J. Petea". This donatio
2 CONC n is noted in a map of early missions found @ www.macomb.lib.mi.us/mountclemens/inages/lansemap.jpg.
