1 NOTE {geni:about_me} The couple lived for some years along the Detroit River on the South Shore (the Windsor side).  Fr. Simple Bocquet, the priest at St. Anne's church in Detroit arranged for Fr. P. Potier, S.J., the missionary to the
2 CONC  Hurons in Windsor, to marry the couple, as they did not want to risk the dangerous crossing of the River to get to St. Anne's.
