1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Mrs. LeBoeuf left Tomahawk on 6 September 1910 to visit her sons Alphonse and Oscar in Gary, Indiana. She was there 5 weeks. While there she helped care for a former Tomahawk resident who was ill with typhoid fever
2 CONC . She next travelled to Detroit to visit her son Herman. After one week in Detroit she became ill with typhoid pneumonia and was hospitalized for 12 week. She was slowly recovering and doing well when other complications developed
2 CONC , necessitating surgery. She had surgery on 5 January, 1911 and died two days later. She had specifically instructed her family she wished to be buried in Tomahawk so her body was retured by train from Windsor, Canada, where a wak
2 CONC e was held for her Canadian siblings.
2 CONT
2 CONT She married Noe LeBoeuf on 19 October, 1880 in Windsor, Ontario, Canada. In the spring of 1890 the family moved to Tomahawk from Detroit. She was the mother of 4 sons and 4 daughters.
