1 NOTE {geni:about_me} [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/251993333/pierre_descomps_dit_labadie Find a Grave]
2 CONT
2 CONT "992?/3530 West Jefferson ave (Formally River road) also known as the Labadie house. According to the City of Detroit Michigan  1701-1922, Volume 2 this house was built in 1786. It was considered the oldest house in Detroit for ma
2 CONC ny years, It was built as a log cabin that had been modified over time. The round bay rooms you see on the side of the house were built on in 1831. according to the Burton Historical collection  It stood on the American side of th
2 CONC e river and the logs of which it was built received a shower of bullets during the War of 1812. and shortly after that it was covered up in clapboard siding. It's said Pierre Labadie was the one that built this house. Theirs a lot
2 CONC  of history in regards to Labadie family in regards to this house that I can't fit in this description! the house stood standing until 1910 and it was Demolished to make room for a Gas reservoir tank. Another house I covered on he
2 CONC re the Stephen Moore Residence 967/3511 Fort Street Sat right behind this house! Image credits, the first image is from the Library of congress dated unknown. the second image is from the Burton Historical collection supposedly ta
2 CONC ken before it was torn down in 1910."  Mark Conett II. Facebook post on Detroit Historical Architecture group's page. Dec 2016
2 CONT
2 CONT See photo.
