2 CONT
2 CONT Alexis DESCOMPS DIT LABADIE [Parents] was born on 3 Apr 1746 in Detroit, Wayne County, Michigan. He died on 19 Apr 1816 in Detroit, Wayne County, Michigan. He was buried on 20 Apr 1816 in Detroit, Wayne County, Michigan. He marrie
2 CONC d Mary Frances ROBERT on 26 Feb 1770 in Detroit, Wayne County, Michigan.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary Frances ROBERT was born on 4 Feb 1752 in Detroit, Wayne County, Michigan. She died on 2 May 1821 in Detroit, Wayne County, Michigan. She was buried on 3 May 1831 in Detroit, Wayne County, Michigan. She married Alexis DESCOMPS
2 CONC  DIT LABADIE on 26 Feb 1770 in Detroit, Wayne County, Michigan. [http://www.chambersheritage.com/pafg443.htm#14273 '''read more....''']
2 CONT
2 CONT BAKER FARM Private Claim No.: 24 Width:2 arpents (384 ft) Area: 67.37 acres Earliest known owner: Pierre Descomps Labadie (1702-1782) 1 April 1750--Government of New France confirmed land claim of Pierre Descomps Labadie. 1782--La
2 CONC badie died, leaving land to son Alexis Descomps Labadie. 16 July 1807--Detroit land office recorded private claim #24 by Labadie. 20 April 1811--Private claim #24 confirmed. 4 April 1816--Sold to Labadie's son-in-law and daughter,
2 CONC  Louis and Cecile LeDuc. 25 March 1822--Sold to Robert A. Forsyth. 16 December 1823--Sold to Colonel Daniel Baker of the U.S. Army. October 1836--Baker submitted a plat of his farm south of Michigan Avenue several days before his 
2 CONC death. 1845--Executors of Baker's estate prepared a plat for the north portion of the farm. Corktown history
