1 NOTE {geni:about_me} From the book "Wisconsin's Early French Habitants" by Jo Bartels Alderson and Kate Alderson Rennert: Joseph Parent, the son of Laurent Parent and Jeanne Cardinal married Marie Catherine the daughter of Jean Baptist
2 CONC e Cuillerier dit Beaubean and Marie Anne Lootman dit Barrois on 18 Nov. 1771 in Detroit.
2 CONT
2 CONT "Joseph's recollections of the Pontiac War form the basis of histories of that event".
2 CONT
2 CONT (Ray Parent) the recollections were written down by Lewis Cass and were utilized by Francois Parkman in the story of the Pontiac War.  (The Geneology of the French Families of the Detroit River 1701 - 1936, By Cristian Dennissen
2 CONT
2 CONT From this we must conclude that he was an eye witness.
