2 CONT Guillaume Jr. a pilot on the Saint-Lawrence died tragically with an apprentice named, Saint-Laurent and another pilot, Amable Lavoie (who survived), on the ship &quot;Camillus&quot;. On June 27, 1820, while piloting with these two
2 CONC  men, he went up on deck during a storm and disappeared overboard. From Guillaume, junior, descends Doctor Jean-August Ross, who was a liberal federal representative from Rimouski from 1897 to 1911, under Sir Wilfrid Laurier.
