1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Daniel Joseph (Daniel) Amiot dit Villeneuve formerly Amyot aka Amiot, Villeneuve
2 CONT
2 CONT Son of Mathieu (Amiot) Amiot dit Villeneuve and Marie Miville
2 CONT
2 CONT Brother of Charles (Amiot) Amiot dit Villeneuve, Pierre (Amiot) Amiot dit Villeneuve, Anne Marie Amiot, Marguerite (Amyot) Amiot dite Villeneuve, Jean Baptiste Amiot, Marie Françoise Amiot, Jean Amiot, Catherine Ursule Amyot, Math
2 CONC ieu Amiot, Philippe (Amiot) Amiot dit Lerpinière, Marie Jeanne Amiot, Étienne Amiot, Marie Françoise Amiot and Geneviève Amiot [half]
2 CONT
2 CONT Husband of Domitille Marie Kapeouapnokoue — married 2 Sep 1709 in Montréal, Canada, Nouvelle-France
2 CONT
2 CONT Father of Marie (Amiot dit Villeneuve) Villeneufve, Anne Amiot dit Villeneuve and Marie Louise Thérèse (Villeneuve) Amiot dit Villeneuve
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Biography'''
2 CONT Daniel (Amyot) Amiot dit Villeneuve lived in Canada, New France.
2 CONT Daniel Joseph Amyot was born on October 4, 1665, and baptized on the 5th in Quebec City (ND), son of Mathieu Amyot and Marie Myville; his godfather was Daniel de Courcelle, governor for the King in this country, his godmother Mari
2 CONC e Barbe de Boullongne, widow of the late Monsieur d'Ailleboust[1].
2 CONT
2 CONT Census 1666: Québec
2 CONT Mathieu Amiot dit Villeneuve, 37, resident; Marie Miville, 33, his wife; Charles, 14; Pierre, 13; Anne-Marie. 11; Marguerite, 9; Jean-Baptiste, 8; Jean, 6; Françoise, 5; Catherine, 3; Daniel, 6 months; Antoine Ducos, 26, hired ser
2 CONC vant. They live in Quebec City[2].
2 CONT
2 CONT Census 1667: Sillery
2 CONT Mathieu Amyot, 40; Marie Miville, his wife, 35; Charles, 16; Pierre, 15; Anne-Marie, 14; Marguerite, 11; Jean-Baptiste, 9; Françoise, 7; Jean, 6; Catherine-Ursule, 5; Daniel-Joseph, 2; Mathieu, 1 1/2 months; servants: Adrien Saill
2 CONC ot, 19; Daniel Le Roy, 20; 9 cattle, 27 acres in value.[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT Census 1681 - seigneury of Maur
2 CONT Mathieu Amyot 53; Marie Miville, his wife, 50; children: Jean-Baptiste 22, Jean 20, Daniel 16, Mathieu 14, Philippe 13, Marie 8. Catherine 17. Jeanne 11. Marie 6; 3 rifles; 3 horned cattle; 30 acres in value[3].
2 CONT '''Parents''':
2 CONT *Father: Mathieu Amyot
2 CONT *Mother: Marie Myville
2 CONT '''Born''':
2 CONT October 4, 1665 in Québec, Canada, Nouvelle-France[1] Baptized - 5 Oct 1665 Quebec (ND)[4]
2 CONT '''Marriage''': 
2 CONT *Domitille Oukabe dite Neveu \ Domithilde LA FOURCHE, (Fort Détroit, New France, now Michigan) ??
2 CONT Daniel Joseph Amiot dit Villeneuve, aged 43, married Marie Kape8apnok8e, 8ta8aise in nation, on 9 Sep 1709 in Notre-Dame de Montréal [5][6]
2 CONT '''Children'''
2 CONT *Daniel (de Villeneuve ) AMIOT b: in Michillimakinak, (Mackinaw), New France (now Michigan)
2 CONT *Nanette VILLENEUVE b: in Mackinac, New France (now Michigan)
2 CONT *Jean Baptiste Ambroise AMIOT b: 1694
2 CONT *Daniel (Amiot) DE VILLENEUVE b: ABT. 27 Sep 1712 in Michilimackinac
2 CONT *Anne AMOIT-VILLENEUVE b: 8 Mar 1714/15 in Mackinac
2 CONT *Marie Louise Therese (Outaquais) VILLENEUVE b: ABT. 10 Jan 1719/20 in Mackinac, New France (now Michigan)
2 CONT *Constant (dit Villeneuve ) AMIOT b: 1723 in Mackinac
2 CONT *Agathe (dit Villeneuve ) AMIOT b: 5 Feb 1723/24
2 CONT
2 CONT Mention in parish records with signature
2 CONT
2 CONT Godfather in the following baptism:
2 CONT Joseph Lamoureux was born 7 May 1719. He was the son of François Lamoureux seigneur de Bellevue and his wife Marguerite Menard. He was baptized 9 May 1719 in Ste-Anne-de-Bellevue, godparents were Daniel Amyot de Villeneuve “demeur
2 CONC ant au fort des sauvages de la mission de St-Louis” (Fort Michilimackinac) and Barbe Lamoureux wife of sieur Boyer, both sign. [7]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Sources'''
2 CONT
