1 NAME Denys /Duquet/
2 GIVN Denys
2 SURN Duquet
2 _MARNM Duquet
2 NICK Dionysio Duquet
2 NICK Denis du Quay
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE DEC 1605
2 ADDR
3 CITY La Rochelle
3 STAE Aunis
3 CTRY France
1 DEAT
2 DATE 26 NOV 1675
2 PLAC Lauzon
2 ADDR
3 CITY Lévis
3 STAE Québec
3 CTRY Canada
1 BURI
2 DATE 27 NOV 1675
2 ADDR
3 CITY Québec (Agglomération)
3 STAE Québec
3 CTRY Canada
1 OCCU fur trader, Soldier, Fur Trader, Immigrant, member of the Taite de Tadoussac
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Denys was born in Piotou, Normandie France about 1605,  Last name was written as Duquay on his marriage certificate in   1638. He had immigrated from France to Canada around the year 1633. As a young man he became 
2 CONC a wealthy fur trader, He married a girl from France on May 13, 1638, she was only 13, but they were married 37 years, till his death in 1675. They had   9 children,  
2 CONT
2 CONT Source ?????  
2 CONT
2 CONT  Is he related to Jeanne Duqué (Duquay Duquet) 2nd wife of Antoine Leboëme ? Denis " Duqué"  was present in Québec at the wedding of Jeanne Leboëme to Charles Achapt, daughter of Antoine from his first marriage to Judith Blanchet,
2 CONC  in 1659.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT 4. Denis Duquet, born Abt. 1605 in Normandie, France; died 27 November 1675 in Quebec, Canada. He was the son of 8. Joseph Duquette and 9. Jeanne Barbie. He married 5. Catherine Gauthier 13 May 1638 in Notre Dame de Quebec. 5. Cat
2 CONC herine Gauthier, born Abt. 1627 in Paris, France; died 03 August 1702 in Canada. She was the daughter of 10. Phillipe Gauthier and 11. Marie Pichon.
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes for Denis Duquet: On March 29, 1649, Denis Duquet obtained land in Quebec.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1659: Denis became a member of the Traite de Tadoussac. This was the embarkation warehouse and trading post from which the furs were sent to France. Denis was noted in the records to be the brother in law or beau-frere, of two pre
2 CONC sidents of the Societe des Habitants.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1660: Denis was named an Honorable Gentleman in this year of 1660.
2 CONT
2 CONT 27 November 1675: From the Parish of Notre-Dame Quebec:
2 CONT
2 CONT On the 27th day of the month of November in the year one-thousand six hundred and seventy five, Denis Duquet, a resident of the coast of Lauzon, died at the age of seventy years. He was living in the hospital of Quebec (and died) 
2 CONC after having received the Holy Sacraments of Last Communion and Extreme Unction. The body was buried the following day in the Cemetery of the Paupers beside the Hospital.
2 CONT
2 CONT More About Denis Duquet: DIT: Desrochers
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage Notes for Denis Duquet and Catherine Gauthier: When Denis and Catherine were married, Denis was about 27 years old. Catherine was about fourteen. Nobelman Pierre Legardeur and M. Noel Jucherau were witnesses.
2 CONT
2 CONT More About Denis Duquet and Catherine Gauthier: Marriage: 13 May 1638, Notre Dame de Quebec
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Denis Duquet and Catherine Gauthier are: i.	Pierre Duquet, born 14 January 1642/43 in Quebec, Canada; died 13 October 1687 in Quebec, Canada; married Anne Lamarre 25 August 1666 in Quebec City, Canada; born 1649 in St.
2 CONC  Sulphice, Paris, France1.
2 CONT
2 CONT More About Pierre Duquet: Baptism Sponsors: Pierre Legardieur de Repitigny/Marguerite Marlin Occupation: Royal Notary Residence (1920): The first Canadian born Notary at age 20
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage Notes for Pierre Duquet and Anne Lamarre: Anne LaMarre was a "Fille du Roi"
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
