2 CONT FRENCH-CANADIAN TRADER OF FOND-DU-LAC WHO MARRIED A HALF-BREED WOMANFROM RED RIVER. TRADER AT FOND DU LAC, LAKE SUPERIOR. MOVED TO SAULTABOUT 1820. DEVIED HAVING INDIAN BLOOD. MOVED TO SAULT ABOUT 1820.
2 CONT
2 CONT Xavier Biron, in 1846, claimed to have occupied the same spot on the north bank of St. Mary's River (Sault Ste Marie) from 1815 to 1846.  He claimed to have written authority from Major Winniett who commanded Drummond Island.
2 CONT
2 CONT May have been called "Alexis"
