1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://gw.geneanet.org/ra41dr07?lang=en;p=jacques;n=messier
2 CONT
2 CONT Male:    Jacques Messier
2 CONT
2 CONT Born about 1649
2 CONT
2 CONT Deceased 22 March 1697 (Friday) - Varennes, cté Verchères, Qc , age at death: possibly 48 years old
2 CONT
2 CONT Buried 24 March 1697 (Sunday) - Varennes, cté Verchères, Qc
2 CONT
2 CONT Parents:
2 CONT
2 CONT David Messier ca 1616-1687
2 CONT
2 CONT Marguerite Barc †1676
2 CONT
2 CONT Spouses and children:
2 CONT
2 CONT Married about 1685 , Québec, Qc, to Marie-Madeleine-Renée Couillard 1670-1695
2 CONT
2 CONT  with
2 CONT
2 CONT Male:   Jacques Messier 1692-
2 CONT
2 CONT Siblings:
2 CONT
2 CONT Male:   Michel Messier ca 1640-1725
2 CONT
2 CONT ------------------------------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.famillemessierfamily.org/#!jacques-messier-e/ccv6
2 CONT
2 CONT Jacques Messier
2 CONT
2 CONT [MTD]
2 CONT
2 CONT ______________________________________
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.genealogy.com/forum/surnames/topics/messier/356/
2 CONT
2 CONT "       10       iv.       Jacques Messier, born about 1649 in Vascoeuil, Normandie, France; died Bef. 23 Nov 1712 in Vercheres, QC.He married Marie-Madeleine-Renee Couillard-dit-Fontaine about 1685 in Unknown (perhaps Montréal), 
2 CONC QC; born 04 Jul 1670 in Québec City, QC; died 16 Jun 1695 in Varennes, QC.
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes for Jacques Messier: It is not clear if at 9 years old, he was the Godfather to his niece Catherine Messier on July 12, 1659 in Montreal.It could just as well have been his uncle Jacques (Catherine’s grand-uncle) that was he
2 CONC r Godfather. Jacques was living with his older brother Michel's family in the Montreal 1666 census. Jacques was about 17 at the time. Jacques and Marie Renee were married after the 1681 census.They had only one child."
2 CONT
2 CONT [MTD]
2 CONT
2 CONT ______________________________________
