2 CONT "Emigration Rochelaise en Nouvelle France"-Godbout pg 39.
2 CONT Tanguay Vol I pg 93-94.
2 CONT Jette pg 180.
2 CONT NOTE:  "Emigration Rochelaise en Nouvelle France"-Godbout pg 39, states:  They were only able to find one "Mathurin Brunet" in the archives at LaRochelle.  It further states that this "Mathurin" married Marie Pajot who was born 15
2 CONC  June 1663.
2 CONT A short bio of Antoine Brunet acquired from the internet (copy filed L-26-14).
2 CONT LDS Ancestral File, family group record of #2387 (copy filed L-26-28)
2 CONT -------------------------------------------------
2 CONT The following was acquired from:  <http://www.linfonet.com/articles/eveil/000304/cron2/index.html< a translated version follows.
2 CONT
2 CONT History Of Our Families
2 CONT Brunet, Brunette
2 CONT aka Belhumeur
2 CONT
2 CONT The newcomer named Antoine Brunet. His father, Mathurin, had married Marie Pagot (Antoine aka Brunet to his marriage) probably about 1633. Originating in the province of Aunis, Antoine is baptized at La Rochelle in 1644. he arrive
2 CONC s in 1662 at Quebec, where one introduces Francoise Moisan to him, daughter of the king. Maître Jean Gloria writes the marriage contract in Quebec on October 19, 1663. On November 28, the couple marries itself religieusement in Vi
2 CONC lle-Marie (Notre-Dame). Antoine cleared three small holdings in lenceinte du Vieux-Montréal. The couple had nine children, including seven girls. We do not know the date of the death of Antoine. Left for France about 1693, he did 
2 CONC not return. Did he die in la Vieille-France or perish at sea? We are unaware of it.
2 CONT
2 CONT It is Francois, baptized on March 17, 1665, which takes the changing. He cultivates a small holding located on the current site of the newspaper the Press. On November 15, 1688, in Boucherville, he marries Anne Ménard. Consequentl
2 CONC y, one finds him at Long-Point, Boucherville and, especially, Lachenaie since 1698. he is at crossed seigniories of Lachenaie and Terrebonne that he cultivates the ground. François and Anne will have 12 children (three boys and ni
2 CONC ne girls). Hehes withdrawn in the new village of Terrebonne of which he becomes one of the first five inhabitants. He dies on July 13, 1739 and is buried in Terrebonne the following day.
2 CONT
2 CONT Brownish Jean-François, born on March 17, 1704 at Lachenaie, takes the changing. He marries Marie-Anne Thibault, in Terrebonne, on February 9, 1728. The couple will have 12 children (five boys and seven girls). Jean-François takes
2 CONC  part, as a colonist, with the rise of the seigniory of Terrebonne. In 1751, the sulpicians of Sault-au-Récollet concede hin with two grounds. Henceforth, the family fixes itself close to the old Indian reserve. The ancestor dies 
2 CONC there on September 16, 1778.
2 CONT
2 CONT The elder one, François-Marie, baptized on November 23, 1728, married Genevieve-Amable Vanier, on May 9, 1757, at Sault-au-Récollet. Fifteen children will be born (eight boys and seven girls). He dies after 1797.
2 CONT
2 CONT The second son, Louis-Gabriel, born on July 4, 1759, married Thérèse Quevillon, at Saint-Vincent-of-Paul (Jesus island), on November 17, 1788. he cultivates the ground of Sault that his father yielded on April 11, 1787 to him. He 
2 CONC dies on July 7, 1825. With Thérèse, he had 17 children (11 boys and six girls).
2 CONT
2 CONT The elder one, Louis, married Marie-Archangel Monciaux (aka Desormeaux) in Saint-Vincent-du-Paul on January 8, 1816. He dies there on September 10, 1848 leaving 13 children (nine boys and four girls).
2 CONT
2 CONT Joseph, the tenth child, is born on November 11, 1829 and dies in Saint-Vincent-du-Paul on December 3, 1904. He marries Domitille Labelle on November 25, 1852 there. The couple has 18 children, also divided between boys and girls.
2 CONC  On May 2, 1908, he sold the ground of Saint-Vincent-du-Paul. This line of Brunet dies out then as Belhumeur farmers.
2 CONT
2 CONT It is in Montreal that one follows Augustin, the ninth child. He is established in the parish Saint-Jean-Baptiste and opens a shop of plumbing. Married to Adélina Lecompte at Saint-Louis-du-France, on January 7, 1890, he had 14 ch
2 CONC ildren: 11 boys and three girls. He died on April 30, 1929.
2 CONT
2 CONT One as of his sons, Auguste, who deserved this nickname of Belhumeur so much and was born on January 24, 1904, was my father. He continued the trade of plumber and, with several of his brothers, assumed the family shop in the stre
2 CONC et Hôtel-de-Ville. He married Olivette Carrier, a girl of Lauzon, on August 10, 1935, in the parish Saint-Alphonse-D' Youville. He died on June 18, 1985.
2 CONT
2 CONT Two still-born children preceded me. I was born on July 12, 1945 in the parish of Notre-Dame-du-Très-Saint-Sacrement, in Montreal. I live at Saint-Eustace now and collaborate with the Society of genealogy.
2 CONT
2 CONT Michel Brunette.
2 CONT mbrunette@clg.qc.ca.
2 CONT
