2 CONT LANDMARKS of DETROIT A History of the City  Robert B Ross & George B Catlin  page 113 
2 CONT
2 CONT ROBERT, Pierre, dit LaFONTAINE.  He moved to Detroit May 19, 1708, with his wife and children.  He had been there before, having come June 15, 1706, in charge of a canoe of merchandise.  His wife was Angelique Ptolomee (or Tholme)
2 CONC .  After he died his widow married Guillaume Bouche, August 16, 1716.   At the marriage of his son Antoine in 1743, this Pierre Robert is referred to as "the late Antoine Robert."  the son married Marie-Louise Becmond.
2 CONT                                       -    -     -    -    -   --   -   Did Angelique also use the dit (surname) DALLONE ?   Or perhaps she really was adopted and DALLONE was her true maiden surname ? 
2 CONT                           -    -    -    -    -    -    -    -    -    Notes for Angelique Ptolomee: Cadillac's Village or "Detroit Under Cadillac." With a list of property owners and a history of the settlement 1701 to 1710. Comp
2 CONC iled by C. M. Burton Detroit, 1896. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Tholme, Angelique, wife of Pierre Robert. This name is given as Angelique Dalonne, and in some places as Ptolme, by Tanguay. She was buried in 1744, aged about 65 years. She married Guillaume Bouche,  after the death of Robert. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Boucher, Guillaume. His first wife was named Jeanne Beauvais, and after her death, in 1703 he married Angelique Tholme, widow of Pierre Robert, August 16, 1716. 
2 CONT                        =    =   =  =  =   =   =    The St-Anges-Gardienschurch parish book record of their marriage lists her [Angelique Ptolme] parents as:  deffunct Charles Ptolme, habitant de Lachine & Marie Magdelenne Moison l
2 CONC a vuefue apresent femme de Louis Fortier habitant de Lachine.... 
2 CONT                    =  =  =  =  =  =  
2 CONT
2 CONT Buried 5 Jun 1744
