1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Cecile and her husband Louis lived on what was known as the Baker Farm, Private Claim No. 24.  The earliest known owner was Pierre Descomps Labadie (1702 - 1782).  On April 1, 1750 the Government of New France conf
2 CONC irmed land claim of Pierre.  In 1782 he died, leaving land to his son, Alexis.  On July 16, 1807 Private claim number 24 by Labadie was recorded by the Detroit Land Office.  On April 20, 1811, private claim number 24 was confirmed
2 CONC .  On April 4, 1816 the land was sold to Alexis' son-in-law, Louis Leduc who was married to Cecile (Labadie).  On March 25, 1822 the land was sold to Robert A. Forsyth.  On December 16, 1823 it was sold to Colonel Daniel Baker of 
2 CONC the U.S. Army.  In October 1836 Baker submitted a plat of his farm South of Michigan Avenue several days before his death.  In 1845 executors of Baker's estate prepared a plat for the North portion of the farm.  Corktown History.b
2 CONC logspot.com
