1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Mosley was the son of Moses and Victoria (Frankhouse) Soncrant. He was a bookkeeper by occupation. He was a resident of Newport, Michigan and died at the University of Michigan Hospital, in Ann Arbor, Washtenaw Cou
2 CONC nty, Michigan. Mosley may not have a marker. Aged 41 years, 8 months, 28 days
2 CONT
2 CONT Moses Jr. as he was known was 24 years old, born and a resident of Newport, Monroe County, Michigan when he was married. His bride Mary Black, born in Germany and a resident of Toledo, Ohio was 26 years old at the time of their ma
2 CONC rriage on August 13, 1896 at Newport. Catholic Priest Fr. Lysen performed the ceremony. Mary's parents were Michael Black and Mary Frankertz. Witnesses for the wedding were Jerome and Elizabeth Sancrainte (spelling in record). Bot
2 CONC h witnesses were residents of Newport, Monroe County, Michigan. (MRMC, Vol 4, pg. 322) The marriage ended in divorce.
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/196634253/mosley_b_soncrant Find a Grave]
