1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * Updated from [http://www.myheritage.com/research/collection-1/myheritage-family-trees?itemId=176470271-1-2887&action=showRecord&indId=externalindividual-0e17eddbe185da84c5147f0272539be4&mrid=10ffdb63714a34519d4f3
2 CONC eaa965166fd MyHeritage Family Trees] via son [http://www.geni.com/profile-34665928665 David Larabelle] by [http://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Oct 29 2014, 0:21:24 UTC''
2 CONT
2 CONT I have now walked this cemetery twice, and another person has done the same. Neither of us has found his grave. However, there are empty spots to the east and west of his wifes' grave (Teresa Chane Larabell). As mentioned on the c
2 CONC emetery page, records here are very poor.
2 CONT
2 CONT His daughter Teresia Larabell Normandin
2 CONT  and many other Normandins are buried just to the north of Teresa Chane Larabell(his wife)
2 CONT
2 CONT Michigan GENDIS has his first name as Antonio...
2 CONT
2 CONT As mentioned on the cemetery page, only the readable graves were transfered from the Old St. Marys Cemetery to this one. It is possible that he is still at the old cemetery site. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Birth date is from the book called the Larabell Calvalcade, by John A. Larabell
2 CONT
2 CONT The photo of the Larabell plot shows his SON, Antoine III
2 CONT
2 CONT This is my 3x ggrandfather.* Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/101141557/antoine-larabell Find A Grave Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Aug 9 2022, 6:50:57 UTC''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT I have now walked this cemetery twice, and another person has done the same. Neither of us has found his grave. However, there are empty spots to the east and west of his wifes' grave (Teresa Chane Larabell). As mentioned on the c
2 CONC emetery page, records here are very poor.
2 CONT
2 CONT His daughter Teresia Larabell Normandin
2 CONT  and many other Normandins are buried just to the north of Teresa Chane Larabell(his wife)
2 CONT
2 CONT Michigan GENDIS has his first name as Antonio...
2 CONT
2 CONT As mentioned on the cemetery page, only the readable graves were transfered from the Old St. Marys Cemetery to this one. It is possible that he is still at the old cemetery site. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Birth date is from the book called the Larabell Calvalcade, by John A. Larabell
2 CONT
2 CONT The photo of the Larabell plot shows his SON, Antoine III
