1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.familysearch.org/en/tree/person/about/LCQW-QYV
2 CONT Brief Life History of Charles
2 CONT
2 CONT When Charles Boucher was born on 12 February 1726, in Sorel-Tracy, Pierre-De Saurel, Quebec, Canada, his father, Charles Boucher, was 35 and his mother, Marie Geneviève Marguerite Henault, was 29. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He married 1st wife Marie Thérèse Hétu (1731-1787) on 1 July 1748, in Saint-Antoine-de-Lavaltrie, Canada, New France. They were the parents of at least 7 sons and 10 daughters. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He married 2nd wife Marie Anne Brisset Dupas (1768–1797)
2 CONT On 1 août 1791 in Sainte-Geneviève-de-Berthier, Berthier, Québec, Canada.
2 CONT No children on record; all of Charles children were with his first wife.
2 CONT
2 CONT He died on 5 June 1811, in Berthierville, D'Autray, Quebec, Canada, at the age of 85, and was buried in Sainte-Geneviève-de-Berthier, Berthier, Quebec, Canada.
