1 OCCU Captain of the 2nd Michigan Militia
1 TITL Captain
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=104849075&ref=wvr
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.riverraisinbattlefield.org/biographies.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT Captain Jean-Baptiste Couture’s home was used as shelter for U.S. troops during the Battle of the River Raisin on January 22, 1813.  When the right wing gave way, he and his son, Medard, rushed out to assist them, but were driven 
2 CONC across the river.  Captain Couture was killed near the home of Joseph Robert, and his son carried the body back to their property to hide it from the Indians.
2 CONT
2 CONT Medard Couture stayed to help the American wounded and was nearly killed himself on January 23, but Waugon, an Ottawa who knew the family, saved him by throwing a blanket over him and proclaiming to his warriors, “Take care of him
2 CONC …  His father lies dead in the yard, and I am now his father.”
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Wikitree profile ID: Couture-146
2 CONT Jean Batiste Couture (Sr) was a Captain in the Michigan Militia during the War of 1812 and his son was a Lieutenant. During the River Raisin Massacre, the senior Jean Baptist was killed, and his son pulled his body into the house,
2 CONC  to keep him from being scalped by indians.  The son was later captured, by the British but was released on giving his word that he would not fight them in the future. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Per findagrave.com:
2 CONT Jean Baptiste Couture was born in Ecorse, Michigan 31 Jan 1764 and baptized the same day at Ste-Anne-de-Detroit.
2 CONT He married Catherine L'enfant 24 Apr 1768 at Ste-Anne-de-Detroit.
2 CONT He was a Captain of the Michigan Militia during the war of 1812 and died 22 Jan 1813 during the Battle of River Raisin inthat war. He was originally buried at Ste Anne Cemetery in Detroit but when that cemetery was closed he was r
2 CONC eburied 25 Aug 1823 at St Antoine, River Raisin.
2 CONT He and Catherine had the following children:
2 CONT Marie Julie (Married Francois Navarre)
2 CONT Catherine (Married James Navarre)
2 CONT Jean Baptiste (Married Angelique Menard & Angelique Reaume)
2 CONT Monique (Married Ambroise Genereux)
2 CONT Dominique (Married Anchange Menard)
2 CONT ==
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
