1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Marguerite was a "fille du roi" or duaghter of the King.
2 CONT
2 CONT These women, known in French as the "fille du roi", agreed to travel to the new settlements in North America and marry a settler there in exchange for a 50 pound dowry from the French King. Of the nearly 1000 women who undertook t
2 CONC he journey, about 800 made it to Canada.
2 CONT
2 CONT They made contracts of marriage with the men who had originally settled the New World and usually married within a few days or weeks of the contract signing. Often the women broke the contracts, only to remake them or make new con
2 CONC tracts with other men.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT http://gw.geneanet.org/ra41dr07?lang=en;p=marguerite;n=raisin
2 CONT
2 CONT F  Marguerite Raisin Born about 1651 - Inconnu Deceased 25 November 1700 (Thursday) - La Prairie, Qc , age at death: possibly 49 years old Buried 25 November 1700 (Thursday) - La Prairie, Qc Spouses and children
2 CONT
2 CONT Married before 22 November 1671 , Lieu indéterminé (PRDH), to Bernard Deniger\Sansoucy ca 1627- with M Jean Deniger 1672-1716 F Marie Deniger ca 1675-1765 M Pierre Deniger\Sansoucy 1677-1730 M René Deniger 1684-1718 Notes
2 CONT
2 CONT Individual Note
2 CONT
2 CONT fille du roi arrivée en 1670/"Daughter of the king" arrived in 1670.
2 CONT
2 CONT ------------------------------------------------------------
