1 CONT According to land patent for Aug 2 1884, Charles had settled to the residence in Redfield, Spink Co Aug 15, 1883. The property had a 12x12 frame house and a well. It was 160 acres of which he planted potatoes & other vegetables. T
1 CONC his was valued at $200.00. The land was purchased at $1.60 per acre.
1 CONT Published in The Dakota Sun, June 13, 1884, a notice was posted that Charles H Druyer had filed notice of his intention to make final proof in support of his claim re: his property.
1 CONT Pension records of 1895 describe him as 45 years old, 5' 8" dark complexion, black hair, gray eyes.
